SUMMARY:David Hockney: Perspective Should Be Reversed Opening Celebration
LOCATION:120 W. Gasparilla Plaza Tampa \, FL 33602 United States
DESCRIPTION:Be among the first to explore the Tampa Museum of Arts newest 
 contemporary exhibition David Hockney: Perspective Should Be Reversed. Joi
 n us for a Curators Chat with Joanna Robotham\, Curator of Modern and Cont
 emporary Art\, as we learn more about one of the most influential and belo
 ved artists of the 20th and 21st centuries. Programming\, gallery access\,
  light bites\, and access to a cash bar included with purchase. David Hock
 ney: Perspective Should Be Reversed presents 60 years of work by acclaimed
  British artist David Hockney (19372026). Drawn from the collections of th
 e Jordan D. Schnitzer and His Family Foundation\, the exhibition features 
 over 140 prints\, collages\, photographs\, and iPad drawings. A comprehens
 ive survey of Hockneys groundbreaking explorations in printmaking\, video\
 , and new media\, Perspective Should Be Reversed highlights the artists si
 gnature motifs. Intimate portraits of friends and family\, bucolic landsca
 pes\, Los Angeles swimming pools\, vibrant interior spaces\, and stage des
 igns present a unique glimpse into Hockneys visual world. \n\nPermalink: h
 ttps://www.tampa.gov/node/193851
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.tampa.gov/node/193851
END:VEVENT
